  "text": "AUSTRALIAN SHIPBUILDING BOARD\nSYDNEY\n9th. June, 1955.\nDear Mr. McFadyen,\nOn behalf of the General Manager and\nstaff of the Board, I have great pleasure in\nextending to you the heartiest of congratula-\ntions for the honour recently conferred upon\nyou by Her Majesty the Queen.\nYours sincerely,\ndem memlea\n(J.C.M. MERRILEES)\nSECRETARY\nC.H. McFadyen, Esq.,\nC.B.E.,\nSecretary,\nDepartment of Shipping & Transport,\n497. Collins Street,\nMELB OUR NE\nVIC.\nMatarich - Arbre de la Vierge.\nTHE STORY GOES THAT IT WAS UMDER THIS FiGTREE\nTHAT MARY MIYA THE INFANT JESUS RESTEO ON THE\nFLIGHT TO EGYPT.",
